load @term/seed/structure/field
  find field

# The real line: the continuum, the complete ordered field, the geometric image of the reals as an unbroken line. It is
# the first rung of the number tower, dimension one, ordered (every real has a definite place left or right of every
# other), and complete (no gaps, every bounded set has a least upper bound). It is the only complete ordered field. In
# the substrate the real line is never a base thing but the mood of many ternary grains, the average over a crowd of
# discrete tones. The form carries the underlying field; the order and completeness are its defining laws.
form real-line
  link field, like field
